  "steps": [
    "Cook the bacon in a large skillet over medium heat until crisp, 8 to 10 minutes. Drain on paper towels, reserving 2 to 3 tbsp fat in the skillet, and crumble once cool.",
    "Season the chicken tenderloins with salt, pepper, onion powder, and smoked paprika.",
    "Cook the chicken in the bacon fat over medium heat until browned and 165°F inside, about 4 to 5 minutes per side. Rest, then slice or chop.",
    "Whisk the mayo, lemon juice, onion powder, garlic powder, dill, smoked paprika, and chives. Add hot sauce until it is as hot as you like, and thin with water if it is too thick.",
    "Arrange the greens on a platter and lay the chicken, bacon, cucumber, tomato, egg, and avocado over the top in rows, avocado last so it does not brown.",
    "Drizzle with the buffalo ranch and finish with green onion."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "The creator also offers a dairy-free dressing made with 1/2 cup blended full-fat coconut milk, 2 tbsp lemon juice, and 1 tsp brown mustard in place of the mayo. Leftover dressing keeps 4 days refrigerated."
  ],
